[38;5;231m⏺[39m I've opened a browser tab with sketches of where the filters could go. The URL is
  [94m]8;id=8r5ifs;http://localhost:49456/?key=3aa0f006be398494039292379809acf0634540ca3868d882ad478e54e1989ecf\http://localhost:49456/?key=3aa0f006be398494039292379809acf0634540ca3868d882ad478e54e1989ecf[39m]8;;\ if it didn't open by
  itself. Sketches use a lot of tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal.

  The tab shows three layouts. Each one has the same filters: event type, a "Failed sign-ins" shortcut, a search box and
  a live "Showing X of Y events" count. Only the position changes:

  - [1mA. Filter bar above the table (my recommendation).[0m All the filters are visible at once and keyboard order is simple.
    It also stacks cleanly on narrow screens (320px wide).
  - [1mB. A "Filter" button that opens a small panel.[0m It takes less space, and the active filters show as tags you can
    remove. Each filter change needs an extra click, and the panel needs extra keyboard handling.
  - [1mC. Controls in the column headers.[0m It uses no extra space, but it's harder to discover and gets crowded on narrow
    screens.

  The sketches are rough wireframes, not final styling. The real version will use only the colors, spacing and
  components from the UI guidelines.

  Have a look and tell me what you think here. You can also click a layout in the browser to select it.

  A housekeeping note: the companion saves its sketches in [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m at the repo root, and [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m doesn't list
  that folder yet. I won't touch [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m unless you ask. I'll just keep that folder out of any commit.

